WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.988
Module ten looks at urban freight, where on-demand delivery is putting new pressure on streets and curbs.

2
00:00:06.888 --> 00:00:17.592
The last mile is the hardest part of logistics: many small, time-critical deliveries, vans double-parked in traffic lanes, and emissions and noise concentrated in dense neighbourhoods.

3
00:00:18.492 --> 00:00:23.830
A freight twin combines fleet positions, loading-bay occupancy and delivery demand by area.

4
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:28.758
Routing optimisation and traffic simulation then test policies and support dispatch.

5
00:00:29.658 --> 00:00:39.194
Typical policies to test are more or smarter loading zones, bookable curb space, micro-hubs served by cargo bikes, delivery time windows and low-emission zones.

6
00:00:40.094 --> 00:00:49.854
The European LEAD project built digital twins for on-demand urban logistics with living labs in six cities, and shared its open tools in a free online course that this module draws on.

7
00:00:50.754 --> 00:00:59.026
A good freight twin measures both sides: delivery time and cost for operators, and the impact on everyone else on the street, from bus delays to emissions.
